earch a list#Configure the default search behavior#Configure default search behavior using a dictionary attribute#Procedure#{4}":[219,224],"#Search a list#Related":[225,230],"#Search a list#Related#{1}":[227,227],"#Search a list#Related#{2}":[228,228],"#Search a list#Related#{3}":[229,230]},"outlinks":[{"title":"Lists in the classic environment","target":"c_UseLists","line":55},{"title":"Enable text searches","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/platform-administration/c_TextSearchesInRecordLists.md","line":60},{"title":"Personal lists","target":"c_PersonalLists","line":62},{"title":"Auto-complete for reference fields","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/platform-administration/c_AutoCompleteForReferenceFields.md","line":135},{"title":"Reference","target":"onboarding-modals-reference","line":135},{"title":"Field types","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/platform-administration/r_FieldTypes.md","line":142},{"title":"Add a property","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/platform-administration/t_AddAPropertyUsingSysPropsList.md","line":201},{"title":"Lists in the classic environment","target":"c_UseLists","line":227},{"title":"Personal lists","target":"c_PersonalLists","line":228},{"title":"Reference","target":"onboarding-modals-reference","line":229}],"metadata":{"title":"Search a list","description":"You can search a list to find information quickly. The list title bar includes options for searching the list. Administrators can enable text searches for any list.The platform supports several wildcard characters to expand and refine search results.The default search behavior in a list is to search for values that are greater than or equal to the value you enter. Administrators can add properties to change the search behavior to use either a contains search or a starts with search by default, instead of a greater than search.Change the default search behavior at the field level by adding an attribute to a field using the system dictionary.","locale":"en-US","canonical_url":"https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/platform-user-interface/t\\_SearchAList.html","release":"australia","topic_type":"task","last_updated":"2026-03-12","reading_time_minutes":4,"breadcrumb":["Lists in the classic environment","Working in the classic environment","Working in Core UI","Configure UIs and portals","Configure user experiences"],"tags":["#platform-user-interface","#type-task"]},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[],"key":"ServiceNowOfficialDocs/platform-user-interface/t_SearchAList.md"},
